# EtChip Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtChip` is a selectable chip component for the eToro design system. It provides a flexible, accessible chip with:

- **Compound component pattern**: `EtChip.Label` and `EtChip.Icon` subcomponents
- **Selection states**: neutral (unselected) and selected with clear visual feedback
- **Built-in animations**: scale animation on press for tactile feedback
- **Haptic feedback**: enabled by default
- **Context-based state sharing**: selection state shared via React Context to subcomponents
- **Flexible interaction**: supports both action chips (`onPress`) and selection chips (`onSelectionChange`)

**Does NOT handle:**

- Navigation logic (use with router/navigation handlers)
- Multiple chip group management (handle selection state in parent)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtChip` (main component)

```tsx
<EtChip
  selected?: boolean              // default: false
  disabled?: boolean              // default: false
  onPress?: () => void
  onSelectionChange?: (selected: boolean) => void
  haptics?: boolean                // default: true
  showCloseOnSelected?: boolean    // default: false — reveals close icon when selected
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
>
  {children}
</EtChip>
```

**Children constraints:**

- Must contain at least one of: `EtChip.Label` or `EtChip.Icon`
- Can contain both `EtChip.Label` and `EtChip.Icon` in any order
- Order of children determines visual layout (icon before label = leading icon, label before icon = trailing icon)
- No string shorthand - must use compound components

**Interaction behavior:**

- Chip is interactive only if `onPress` or `onSelectionChange` is provided
- When interactive, chip is pressable and shows press animations
- When non-interactive (no handlers), chip is disabled and shows static state

### `EtChip.Label`

```tsx
<EtChip.Label
  style?: StyleProp<TextStyle>
>
  {ReactNode}
</EtChip.Label>
```

**Behavior:**

- Automatically styled based on parent chip's `selected` and `disabled` state
- Text color: default = `carbon900`, selected = `carbon050`, disabled = `carbon300` (overrides selected)
- Uses `body-tiny-medium` text variant
- Receives selection + disabled state via `ChipContext` (no prop drilling needed)

### `EtChip.Icon`

```tsx
<EtChip.Icon
  iconName:IconName // required - icon from icon library
/>
```

**Behavior:**

- Automatically colored based on parent chip's `selected` and `disabled` state
- Icon color: default = `carbon900`, selected = `carbon050`, disabled = `carbon300` (overrides selected)
- Fixed size: 16px
- Receives selection + disabled state via `ChipContext` (no prop drilling needed)

## Usage Patterns

### Basic chip (neutral state)

```tsx
<EtChip selected={false}>
  <EtChip.Label>Technology</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

### Selected chip

```tsx
<EtChip selected={true}>
  <EtChip.Label>Technology</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

### Chip with leading icon

```tsx
<EtChip selected={false}>
  <EtChip.Icon iconName="heart" />
  <EtChip.Label>Favorites</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

### Chip with trailing icon

```tsx
<EtChip selected={true}>
  <EtChip.Label>Watchlist</EtChip.Label>
  <EtChip.Icon iconName="watched" />
</EtChip>
```

### Single selection pattern

```tsx
const [selectedCategory, setSelectedCategory] = useState('Technology');

const categories = ['Technology', 'Finance', 'Healthcare', 'Energy'];

{
  categories.map((category) => (
    <EtChip key={category} selected={selectedCategory === category} onSelectionChange={() => setSelectedCategory(category)}>
      <EtChip.Label>{category}</EtChip.Label>
    </EtChip>
  ));
}
```

### Multi-selection pattern

```tsx
const [selectedChips, setSelectedChips] = useState<string[]>(['Technology']);

const toggleChip = (label: string) => {
  setSelectedChips((prev) => (prev.includes(label) ? prev.filter((item) => item !== label) : [...prev, label]));
};

{
  categories.map((category) => (
    <EtChip key={category} selected={selectedChips.includes(category)} onSelectionChange={() => toggleChip(category)}>
      <EtChip.Label>{category}</EtChip.Label>
    </EtChip>
  ));
}
```

### Action chip (non-selection)

```tsx
<EtChip selected={false} onPress={() => handleAddToWatchlist()}>
  <EtChip.Icon iconName="plus" />
  <EtChip.Label>Add to Watchlist</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

### Chip with expandable close icon (filter chips)

```tsx
<EtChip
  selected={isSelected}
  showCloseOnSelected
  onSelectionChange={(selected) => setIsSelected(selected)}
>
  <EtChip.Label>Technology</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

When `showCloseOnSelected` is true, the close slot is always mounted and its `width` (`0` to `22`) + `opacity` animate from `selectedProgress` with `overflow: 'hidden'`. The chip width therefore changes on the UI thread, so sibling chips in a group reflow smoothly each frame — no `LinearTransition` / layout animation. Pressing anywhere on the chip (including the icon) toggles selection via `onSelectionChange`.

### Disabled chip

```tsx
<EtChip selected={false} disabled={true} onPress={() => handlePress()}>
  <EtChip.Label>Disabled Action</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

**Note:** Use `disabled` to explicitly prevent interaction on chips that have handlers. This is useful for conditional disabling based on app state.

### Combined onPress and onSelectionChange

```tsx
<EtChip
  selected={isSelected}
  onPress={() => console.log('Chip pressed')}
  onSelectionChange={(selected) => {
    setIsSelected(selected);
    console.log('Selection changed:', selected);
  }}
>
  <EtChip.Label>Toggle</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

**Note:** Both handlers can be used together. `onSelectionChange` is called first (with toggled state), then `onPress` is called.

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using string children (not supported)

```tsx
// BAD - EtChip doesn't support string shorthand like EtButton
<EtChip selected={false}>Technology</EtChip>
```

**Fix:** Always use compound components:

```tsx
<EtChip selected={false}>
  <EtChip.Label>Technology</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

### ❌ Using subcomponents outside of EtChip

```tsx
// BAD - will throw runtime error
<EtChip.Label>Label</EtChip.Label>

// BAD - will throw runtime error
<EtChip.Icon iconName="star" />
```

**Fix:** Always wrap subcomponents inside `<EtChip>`.

### ❌ Manually styling colors

```tsx
// BAD - bypasses design system and context
<EtChip.Label style={{ color: 'red' }}>Label</EtChip.Label>
```

**Fix:** Colors are automatically managed based on `selected` state via context. Use `style` prop only for layout adjustments, not color overrides.

### ❌ Using arbitrary components as children

```tsx
// BAD - only EtChip.Label and EtChip.Icon are valid children
<EtChip selected={false}>
  <View>
    <Text>Custom content</Text>
  </View>
</EtChip>
```

**Fix:** Use only `EtChip.Label` and `EtChip.Icon` as children.

### ❌ Managing selection state incorrectly

```tsx
// BAD - onSelectionChange provides the new state, don't toggle again
<EtChip
  selected={isSelected}
  onSelectionChange={() => setIsSelected(!isSelected)} // Wrong!
>
  <EtChip.Label>Toggle</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

**Fix:** `onSelectionChange` receives the new selected state as a parameter:

```tsx
<EtChip selected={isSelected} onSelectionChange={(selected) => setIsSelected(selected)}>
  <EtChip.Label>Toggle</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

### ❌ Disabling haptics unnecessarily

Only disable haptics when explicitly required (e.g., rapid-fire actions or accessibility preferences):

```tsx
// OK - rapid toggle doesn't need haptics
<EtChip haptics={false} onPress={handleQuickToggle}>
  <EtChip.Label>Toggle</EtChip.Label>
</EtChip>
```

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides theme colors for styling (border, background, text colors)
- `EtText` - underlying text component for `EtChip.Label`
- `EtoroIcon` - underlying icon component for `EtChip.Icon`
- `ChipContext` - React context for sharing `selected` state with subcomponents
- `ChipProvider` - context provider that wraps the chip container
- `useChipState` - hook managing press handlers, animations, and haptics

### External Dependencies

- `expo-haptics` - haptic feedback on press
- `react-native` - `Pressable`, `View`, `StyleSheet`
- `react-native-reanimated` - scale animation on press (Animated.View, useSharedValue, useAnimatedStyle, withSpring)

### Design System Integration

- Colors come from theme (`useEtoroTheme().colors`) — V2 tokens:
  - Border: `carbon300` (all states)
  - Background: `carbon900` (selected) or `transparent` (default / disabled)
  - Text / Icon: `carbon300` (disabled) → `carbon050` (selected) → `carbon900` (default)
- Typography: `body-tiny-medium` variant for label
- Spacing: `gap: 8`, `paddingHorizontal: 16`, `paddingVertical: 6`
- Border radius: `20` (pill shape)
- Icon size: fixed at `16px`

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Context Architecture

The chip uses a simple context pattern to share selection state:

- `ChipProvider` wraps the container and provides `selected` state via `ChipContext`
- `EtChip.Label` and `EtChip.Icon` use `useChipContext()` to access selection state
- This eliminates prop drilling and ensures subcomponents automatically style based on selection

**File structure:**

```
context/
├── chip-context.tsx      # ChipContext + useChipContext hook
└── chip-provider.tsx     # ChipProvider component
```

### Selection State Management

The chip supports two interaction patterns:

1. **Selection chips**: Use `onSelectionChange` to manage selection state
   - Handler receives the new `selected` boolean value
   - Parent should update state based on this value
   - Visual state updates **optimistically on press** (background, label/icon colors, close icon) before the parent re-renders; reconciles when the `selected` prop confirms
   - Parent `onSelectionChange` is invoked inside `startTransition` so heavy consumer work does not block the optimistic paint
   - Useful for single or multi-selection scenarios

2. **Action chips**: Use `onPress` for non-selection actions
   - Handler is called on press
   - `selected` prop can be used for visual state (e.g., "added to favorites")
   - Useful for actions like "Add to Watchlist", "Remove", etc.

3. **Combined**: Both handlers can be used together
   - `onSelectionChange` is called first with toggled state
   - `onPress` is called after
   - Useful when you need both selection tracking and side effects

### Interactive vs Non-Interactive

The chip becomes non-interactive (disabled) when:

- Neither `onPress` nor `onSelectionChange` is provided (implicit)
- The `disabled` prop is set to `true` (explicit)

When non-interactive:

- `Pressable` has `disabled={true}`
- No press animations occur
- No haptic feedback
- Chip displays as a static visual element

Use the `disabled` prop to explicitly disable a chip that has handlers attached (e.g., based on app state).

### Animation Behavior

Every selection visual is driven on the UI thread by a single `selectedProgress` shared value (`0` = unselected, `1` = selected), so React re-renders never interrupt the motion:

- **Press in / out**: Scales to `0.975` and back with spring animation (`damping: 50`, `stiffness: 500`)
- **Selection transition** (`withTiming`, 200ms):
  - **Background**: `interpolateColor(selectedProgress)` from `transparent` to `carbon900`
  - **Label color** (`EtChip.Label`): `Animated.Text` with `interpolateColor(selectedProgress)` from `carbon900` to `carbon050` (static `carbon300` when disabled)
  - **Icon color** (`EtChip.Icon`): two stacked icon layers (`carbon900` + `carbon050`) cross-faded by opacity from `selectedProgress` (SVG fill is a prop, not animatable, so a cross-fade is used). Disabled renders a single static `carbon300` icon
  - **Close icon reveal** (`showCloseOnSelected`): the close slot is always mounted and its `width` (`0` to `22`) + `opacity` animate from `selectedProgress` with `overflow: 'hidden'`. The chip width therefore changes on the UI thread, so sibling chips in a group reflow smoothly each frame — no `LinearTransition` / layout animation
- `selectedProgress` is animated imperatively on press (immediate, UI thread) and reconciled to the confirmed `selected` prop; optimistic React state only feeds `accessibilityState.selected`
- Animation is handled by `useChipState`, `EtChipRoot`, and the `EtChip.Label` / `EtChip.Icon` subcomponents using `react-native-reanimated`

### Haptic Feedback

Haptic feedback is enabled by default (`haptics={true}`):

- Triggers `ImpactFeedbackStyle.Light` on press
- Only fires when chip is interactive (has `onPress` or `onSelectionChange`)
- Can be disabled with `haptics={false}` prop

### Accessibility

The chip includes built-in accessibility support:

- `accessibilityRole="button"` - announces as button to screen readers
- `accessibilityState={{ selected }}` - communicates selection state
- `accessibilityLabel` - custom label for screen readers
- `testID` - for testing purposes

### Visual States

The chip has three visual states:

1. **Neutral (unselected)**:
   - Border: `carbon300`
   - Background: `transparent`
   - Text/Icon: `carbon900`

2. **Selected**:
   - Border: `carbon300`
   - Background: `carbon900`
   - Text/Icon: `carbon050`

3. **Disabled** (only when `disabled={true}` is passed explicitly):
   - Border: `carbon300`
   - Background: `transparent` (selected variant also collapses to transparent visually because text/icon flatten to `carbon300`)
   - Text/Icon: `carbon300`

Colors automatically switch based on `selected` and `disabled` props, and subcomponents receive both via context. A chip that is non-interactive only because no handler was passed (a "static" chip) keeps the default colors — only the explicit `disabled` prop triggers the disabled visuals.

### Children Order Matters

The order of `EtChip.Icon` and `EtChip.Label` children determines visual layout:

- Icon before Label = leading icon (icon on left)
- Label before Icon = trailing icon (icon on right)

The chip uses `flexDirection: 'row'` with `gap: 8` for spacing.

## Related Context

- `EtChipsGroupV2 (chips-group-v2/)` - **Use for chip groups** with built-in selection logic, scroll/wrap layouts, and fade overlays. Recommended over manually mapping `EtChip` for common filter/category patterns.
- `EtText (et-text.tsx)` - EtText component used internally for `EtChip.Label`
- `EtoroIcon (et-icon.tsx)` - EtoroIcon component used internally for `EtChip.Icon`
- `EtButton (button/et-button.tsx)` - Similar compound component pattern (but supports string shorthand)
- `api/types.ts` - Type definitions for `EtChipProps`, `ChipIconProps`, `ChipLabelProps`, `EtChipChildren`
- `context/` - Context architecture for state sharing
- `hooks/use-chip-handlers.ts` - State management and animation logic

### When to Use EtChip vs EtChipsGroupV2

| Scenario                      | Component        |
| ----------------------------- | ---------------- |
| Single standalone chip        | `EtChip`         |
| Action chip (button-like)     | `EtChip`         |
| Custom layout/behavior needed | `EtChip`         |
| Group of filter chips         | `EtChipsGroupV2` |
| Category selector             | `EtChipsGroupV2` |
| Horizontal scrolling list     | `EtChipsGroupV2` |
| Multi-row wrapped chips       | `EtChipsGroupV2` |
